# The stretch of a guess reaches from the read of a method to its call across the arguments, which are walked in both arms
# (the-arguments-of-a-call-stand-between-the-read-of-the-method-and-the-call.ir). Where the arguments hold a method call on ANOTHER receiver, the closed arm of each level
# walked all the levels inside it again: the build grew with the square of the depth (128 deep: +369 M instructions, +475 KB).
# The read of another receiver's method for its call ends the stretch: the innermost call alone is reached across its arguments.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: = ShapeTest {{*}}layouts=[L0]
# CHECK-NOT: = ShapeTest
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell globalThis.hide = value => value;
# ANSWERS: 2 8
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
